  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.0.61\"\n\npackage:\n  name: openinterpreter\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/openinterpreter/openinterpreter/archive/refs/tags/rust-v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 1cbb079f1ac1dcdd569cece1fa4c81d9e8fb65360acb1d554cde06b59fd76040\n  patches:\n    - patches/0001-isolate-conda-package-layout.patch\n    - patches/0002-use-auditable-locked-package-builds.patch\n    - patches/0003-increase-chatgpt-recursion-limit.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    env:\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP: symbols\n      CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI: \"true\"\n    file: build\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - python >=3.11\n    - just\n    - git\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cargo-auditable\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - pkgconf\n    - openssl\n  host:\n    - ${{ 'libcap' if linux }}\n    - ${{ 'openssl' if unix }}\n    - ripgrep\n  run:\n    - ripgrep\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - i\n        - interpreter\n        - openinterpreter-code-mode-host\n      files:\n        - openinterpreter-package.json\n        - ${{ 'openinterpreter-path/rg.exe' if win else 'openinterpreter-path/rg' }}\n        - if: linux\n          then: openinterpreter-resources/bwrap\n        - if: unix\n          then: openinterpreter-resources/zsh/bin/zsh\n        - if: win\n          then:\n            - openinterpreter-resources/codex-command-runner.exe\n            - openinterpreter-resources/codex-windows-sandbox-setup.exe\n        - etc/pixi/i/global-ignore-conda-prefix\n        - etc/pixi/interpreter/global-ignore-conda-prefix\n        - etc/conda/test-files/openinterpreter/0/test_package.py\n      strict: true\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - codex\n        - python >=3.11\n    files:\n      recipe:\n        - test_package.py\n    script:\n      - codex --version\n      - i --version\n      - interpreter --help\n      - openinterpreter-code-mode-host --help\n      - python test_package.py\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://openinterpreter.com\n  documentation: https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal\n  repository: https://github.com/openinterpreter/openinterpreter\n  summary: A lightweight coding agent for open models like Deepseek, Kimi, and Qwen\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  description: |\n    **Open Interpreter** lets LLMs run code (Python, JavaScript, Shell, and more) locally.\n    You can chat with Open Interpreter through a ChatGPT-like interface in your terminal by running `$ interpreter` after installing.\n\n    This provides a natural-language interface to your computer's general-purpose capabilities:\n\n    - Create and edit photos, videos, PDFs, etc.\n    - Control a Chrome browser to perform research\n    - Plot, clean, and analyze large datasets\n    - ...etc.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - eunos-1128\n",
